# Anything holding your own network's data must never be committed.
# Extracted files, cached analysis and cleaned exports. Anchored to the root:
# unanchored, this also matched analyzer/data/, which holds shipped reference
# data and silently failed to commit.
/data/
# Support files themselves:
*.tgz
# A support file that was extracted in place next to the code:
support-*/
# Support files staged for the container to import at start-up. The directory
# itself is kept, so a fresh clone has somewhere to put them and Docker does
# not have to create it:
import/*
!import/.gitkeep
# Your own container settings, which name paths on your machine:
.env
# The published screenshots are made from cleaned data and are kept:
!docs/screenshots/

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
